From 257ff003bf679b7e62d6740471ca619ab6539057 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rawdanger-recomp <rawdanger-recomp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:32:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rawdanger-recomp v0.9.0: orbit camera and fixed cameras off
 (host calls)

PS2_CAMERA_ORBIT: host call at the follow camera's height step turns the camera
round the pivot through the game's own height-over-pivot (+0x354 + look-at offset
+0x3B8) and ground distances (+0x360/+0x364), keeping the distance; mouse up/down
goes straight in as a turn. keys.ini camera_orbit, Settings > Controls.

PS2_FREE_CAMERA: host call replaces the per-frame 'run the active camera' call;
with the setting on, a fixed camera (mode 10) while playing and with no cutscene
bars for a second is switched to the follow camera. keys.ini free_camera (off).
gs: ms_since_cinema_bars().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QNLFPekqhcU2dj7B3Utmea
